Subject: remove '-fno-inline-functions' compile options

`-fno-inline-functions` is a compilation option intended for GCC in the project conf of tizen-base-dev.
LLVM recognizes this option, but its handling is completely different from GCC's.
This causes projects built with LLVM to have no function inlining at all, severely degrading the performance of the resulting binaries.
This is the reason why the LLVM build time on the x86_64 architecture was excessively long.(https://quickbuild.tizen.org/build/1182759)

